WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.159
Speaker 1: I want to play a clip for you today
from C-SPAN.

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:12.370
Now, C-SPAN is not a place where you necessarily
expect the most sort of unhinged political

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.370
discussions.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:19.619
C-SPAN generally does a good job of moderating
relatively sober and respectful discussion.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.010
Even when kind of kooky people call in, they
tend to do a pretty good job with it.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:30.250
Well, during the show Washington Journal on
C-SPAN recently, there was a caller from Tennessee

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:36.909
and that caller called in upset that there
were minorities on his TV screen giving opinions.

00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:39.410
And he said he doesn't like it.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.600
He wants to go back to the way things kind
of used to be.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.649
And for those who are only listening to this
clip, there's an Asian guy and a black woman

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:50.579
who are on the panel on Washington Journal.

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:53.659
And the guy is Nicholas Wu from Politico.

00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:57.739
The woman is Ebony McMorris from the American
Urban Radio Network.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:00:59.979
And take a look at this and then we'll discuss
it.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:00.979
This is really something.

00:01:00.979 --> 00:01:01.979
Speaker 2: Comment for them, please.

00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:06.450
Speaker 3: When I was a little boy, listen,
I'm 83 years old when I was a little boy.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.800
Speaker 1: But I think that, by the way, I
think the caller is a man, although although

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.980
maybe not, I don't know.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:12.980
Speaker 2: Okay.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:13.980
We're going to stop it there.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.980
Let's go to Nancy.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.980
Apologize for that.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:16.980
Speaker 1: I'm sorry.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:17.980
And I didn't even started at the beginning.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:18.980
Let's go to the beginning.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:19.980
I apologize.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:25.300
Speaker 3: Current things here in America
that's going on, particularly in the press

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.640
and the politics of America.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:38.780
I want to know if we could cut out some of
this, if we could cut out some of these these

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:46.000
liberal things that are going on in America,
just like on the TV now we have two minorities

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.280
and I'm not sure minorities.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.280
I'm 83 years.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.280
Speaker 2: Taller.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.440
This that's that shouldn't be a factor.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.500
And the guests that we invite to our program,
which we did invite.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.100
So what's your question or comment for them,
please?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.030
Speaker 3: I was a little bored.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.759
Listen, I'm 83 years old.

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:00.850
I was a little boy.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.500
The colored people here.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.740
Speaker 2: Okay, we're going to stop it there.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.740
Let's go to Nancy.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.760
Apologize for that.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.760
Now.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:11.599
Speaker 1: The colored people are bothering
this 83 year old man or woman.

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:16.239
Now, I know many people will react to this
by saying this is an 83 year old.

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:18.079
These are not common views.

00:02:18.079 --> 00:02:25.260
Well, the issue here is that these are actually
relatively these are more common views than

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.110
we would like to admit.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.469
But a lot of younger people realize you can't
say that out loud.

00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:36.689
You're not supposed to out loud say, I'm really
bothered by all these non white people I'm

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:41.499
seeing in movies and on television and they
even sometimes just call it woke.

00:02:41.499 --> 00:02:48.079
I mean, woke for some people has become a
paraphrase in a sense, for I'm seeing a lot

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:53.170
of liberals with different identities participating
and being allowed to give opinions.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:54.360
And I don't like that now.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:03:00.769
Ebony McMorris, who was the black woman on
the panel, she tweeted after the fact, quote,

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:07.220
I was trying to hold it in, but I promise
you, I felt all my ancestors rushed through

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.440
my body.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.019
Nicholas Wu was right.

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:13.159
Pedro was a master at intercepting that.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.590
Next time the response may be different.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:21.420
And this is really you know, the person says,
I don't I don't have a problem with minorities

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.569
or what they're kind of saying is I'm not
a racist.

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:29.959
I just don't want minorities on my TV screen
giving me political opinions.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:34.310
I don't want to many minorities in my government
or in my neighborhood or in the same waiting

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.730
rooms as me type of moment.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:43.180
And what really makes me kind of sad, it bums
me out the looks on the faces of the guests.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:49.809
There's a bit of I've dealt with this before
sort of look and that is that that's that's

00:03:49.809 --> 00:03:50.809
sad.

00:03:50.809 --> 00:03:51.809
It really is.

00:03:51.809 --> 00:03:55.510
And so when we talk about well, when they
say that they're conservative.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.409
What do they want to conserve or what is what
do they want to go back to?

00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:01.669
Because for many of them, they believe we've
already gone too far.

00:04:01.669 --> 00:04:02.999
They want conserving means.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:03.999
Actually, let's go back.

00:04:03.999 --> 00:04:08.709
We often say vaguely, well, they want to go
back to sort of the fifties, right, where,

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:16.209
yes, there were minorities around, but they
were much more it was much more okay to openly

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:18.209
say these are second tier people.

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:19.250
They're not like us.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:26.480
Yes, women were around, but they were much
more stringently subservient to men.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.440
They're talking about the fifties.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:34.800
And if this is an 83 year old caller, 1955,
they would have been about six years old.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.180
That is exactly what they are kind of thinking
back to.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.180
And this is different.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:45.720
This is what is also fascinating is because
of the Trump era, we're really used to the

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:53.340
neo reactionary, cartoonish conservative JFK
Jr, still alive and QAnon and this type of

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.590
stuff.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:05:02.970
This is much more the 1950s conservative that
we would see a lot more like in the Bush era,

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:06.931
when they would talk about the Moral Majority
and getting back to God and Christianity and

00:05:06.931 --> 00:05:08.380
all these different things.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:14.690
That's this caller this is not really it doesn't
sound to me a Trump histrionic, neo reactionary.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:17.080
It's more of of that and it's quite sad.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.270
And it's still around 83 years old, but it's
still around.

